    {
      "name": "D17",
      "label": "GPIO17 (Led active high)",
      "codeName": "D17",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "led_high"
      ],
      "notes": "PIN_LED — onboard 'User LED' (D2, blue), active-high. Confirmed by tracing the KiCad schematic (github.com/0xCB-dev/0xCB-Helios rev1.0/helios.kicad_sch): net 'LED' runs from RP2040 GPIO17 straight to D2's anode; D2's cathode returns through R15 (1k) to GND, so driving GPIO17 HIGH sources current through the LED to ground (lights it). digital_input dropped to match this repo's led_high precedent for dedicated onboard LED pins (rpipico, vccgnd_yd_rp2040); pwm_output kept for brightness dimming via analogWrite()."
    },
