      "name": "D25",
      "label": "GPIO25 (Led Neopixel)",
      "codeName": "D25",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_output",
        "led_neopixel"
      ],
      "notes": "PIN_NEOPIXEL — dedicated, level-shifted NeoPixel/WS2812 data-out pin (net 'RGB_DO'). Confirmed by tracing the KiCad schematic: GPIO25 feeds pin A of U5 (SN74LVC1T45DRL single-bit level translator) whose DIR pin is hard-wired to +3V3 (fixed A-to-B direction, not auto-sensing), shifting the signal to 5V for driving an external addressable-RGB LED chain. Output-only dedicated hardware — confirmed by vendor marketing ('a 5V level shifted pin to drive RGB LEDs (GP25)... perfect for driving addressable RGB LEDs with 5V signals'). digital_input and pwm_output dropped to match this repo's led_neopixel precedent (vccgnd_yd_rp2040 GPIO23)."
    },
